{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done.\n\nChanged:\n- `flakyqueue/scheduler.py`\n- wrote `out/root_cause.md`\n\nFixes:\n- `add()` now uses the injected clock once for both `created_at` and `run_at`\n- `ready()` now uses the injected clock\n- `schedule_retry()` now uses the injected clock and injected random source\n- removed the random shuffle\n- made ready-task ordering deterministic with:\n  - priority desc\n  - `run_at`\n  - `created_at`\n  - `id`\n\nWhy it was flaky:\n- code mixed injected deps with `time.time()` and `random.random()`\n- equal-priority tasks were shuffled before a stable sort, so tie order stayed random\n\nVerification:\n- `python3 -m pytest tests` could not run here because `pytest` is not installed in this env\n- ran the test functions directly: all passed\n- repeated the key deterministic checks 100 times: all passed\n\nFiles:\n- `/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py`\n- `/workspace/out/root_cause.md`"}}
